  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scope": "The ORIGINAL residualCoefficient*zetaPrimeLogKernel carrier now has both signed bounds on complete ordinary-prime periods, with its factorial kernel, 1-boundedShare allocation, both Riesz hinges, full product phase and ALL factorial orders retained. Cofactors are squarefree with at least two prime factors; there is no upper prime-count restriction. Exact unused-majority allocations give nonnegative marked-order coefficients bounded by the binomial coefficients, independently of the marked prime. Signed finite Abel tails pay a varying amplitude by Q=a*(4W/a^2+D*h*B)^2+h*((W+D*h)*B)^2, where h=2*pi/|y| and B=2/(|y|*a)+4/a^2, for a>=5000 and |y|>=54. The actual factorial amplitude has W_j=exp(-a/2)*(a+h)^j and D_j=W_j*(abs(j/a-1/2)+j*h/a^2). Binomial variance sums every order into the explicit summedPeriodCost, with no maximum-score or order-count multiplier. One proved but UNEVALUATED E>0 gives both signed bounds sqrt(E)*summedPeriodCost and finite-family bound sqrt(E)*sum_i summedPeriodCost_i. Complete periods must lie in the eligible set and be coprime to every selected cofactor. Cofactor-dependent prime holes and the total source-normalized cost remain OPEN; this is NOT a whole-carrier smallness theorem. The optional numerical diagnostic shows a smaller order budget but central-saddle source growth persists; it proves neither an asymptotic no-go nor a lower bound on the signed carrier. No zero or simplicity hypothesis, generic density transport, low-order deletion or extra paid-sector credit is used. Both whole -79/1000 floor and 3/2 ceiling remain open; no zero exclusion or RH claim.",
